            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Love and Human Emotion</strong><br>\nStendhal's analysis of love and human emotion was revolutionary. His book \"On Love\" details his theory of crystallization and the processes involved in falling in love, revealing his acute perception of human psychology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political and Social Commentary</strong><br>\nHis writing often addressed the political climate and social issues of his time, using irony and satire to critique the status quo. Stendhal believed in the potential of literature to influence society by exposing its flaws.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nStendhal died in Paris in 1842. His legacy has grown posthumously, with his novels appreciated for their realism and for the depth of their analysis of the human condition. He is considered one of the earliest and foremost practitioners of realism in French literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
